```

and then

```
type SpecDevices struct {
    // Attributes defines shared attributs for all devices.
	Attributes map[QualifiedName]DeviceAttribute `json:"attributes,omitempty" protobuf:"bytes,1,rep,name=attributes"`

	// Devices lists some or all of the devices in this pool.
	//
	// Must not have more than 128 entries.
	//
	// +optional
	// +listType=atomic
	Devices []Device `json:"devices" protobuf:"bytes,2,name=devices"`
```

I suspect we are not keen on that, but if we are, we need to do it now.  I am OK to hold off on shared attribs, I just don't want to "forget" and then lose by default.  Not having them from the beginning will make introducing them a bit more dangerous for users, which is why I have them on my to-do list.

