I did some experimenting.

It looks like comments that are not directly attached to types or fields do not get propagated into docs, so putting such comments at the end of a type or "detached" should be OK?

It also looks like any comment with a `// +<anything>` form will be filtered out, so perhaps we can invent another convention:

```
// This field is blah blah blah
// +optional
// +// this is an implementation note
// +// these will not show up in docs (except godoc)
```

@thockin: is it okay to limit the implementation of `matchAttribute` for a version to a literal string comparison?

In other words, `matchAttribute: driverVersion` only matches when two devices both use "1.0.0", but not when one device uses "1.0.0" and the other "1.0.00".

It is simpler to implement and more efficient. This needs to be documented, either here or under `matchAttribute`. I cannot imagine why vendors would publish the same version using a different string representation, so this shouldn't be a limitation in practice.
